# tool: Config

Read and change the global configuration of the installation, stored at
`~/.aos/config.json`.

## What an agent can and cannot do
Secrets are never returned to an agent: provider keys, the API token, the
session secret and the tunnel token come back as a fingerprint, never in full.
An agent may change region and general preferences; anything under `security`,
any provider key and the tunnel token are refused with a call to action pointing
the human at the app.

Composite tool `Config` with 2 actions: get, update.

Reading the configuration is safe. Changing it affects every workspace of this installation.

## Usage
Call as `Config({ action: "<action>", input: { ... }, _reasoning: "..." })`.
Set `schema: true` on the same level as `action` to receive the full action detail (description, examples, input schema, token estimate) instead of executing.

## actions

### config_get

Read the configuration, with secrets redacted.

Read the whole configuration.

Every secret is replaced by a fingerprint — enough to tell which key is
configured, useless to whoever reads it. `reveal` is honoured only for a human
on an interactive terminal; an agent that asks for it is refused.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "reveal": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Show secret values in full. Only honoured for a human on an interactive terminal; an agent never receives unredacted secrets."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### config_update

Change configuration fields by dotted path.

Change one or more configuration fields.

Fields are addressed by dotted path, the same path the file shows:
`{"region.timezone": "America/Sao_Paulo"}"`. An agent may only write the
agent-writable allowlist; anything else is refused rather than silently ignored.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "set": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Dotted paths to set, for example {\"region.timezone\": \"America/Sao_Paulo\"}. An agent may only set fields on the agent-writable allowlist.",
      "additionalProperties": true
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "set",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

